  "notes": [
    "The left panel every page wears (the public site, the Products page, the account screen, the products). One source: a page renders these groups in this order, then its own group and 'On this page'.",
    "An entry with 'pane' names a section of the site's home page (the address is the site plus '#' and the pane); 'step' numbers the two remaining Get started steps; 'action' is a control the page provides (the Email Admin dialog, an administrator's page-text editing); 'sub' nests labelled sub-groups inside an entry.",
    "The owner's order (18 Sep 2026): Products leads with Choose a product, which carries the sub-groups Job (Job Search, Interview Preparation) and then Relax (Ask about a Book); User creation follows Products with the Create your account step and the Create Account guide, moved out of Documentation. The steps 'Use it with your own data' and 'Keep improving' were removed with their panes.",
    "A group with 'roles' is carried hidden and shown by the shell script when /__hub/session on the page's own origin answers with a user holding one of those roles. The Account group shows the visitor's name and Sign out for any signed-in visitor.",
    "Job Search views (?view=...) open at the Job Search address the page knows: the public short path here; a page served on the loopback derives them from its directory (apps/hub-portal/src/links.ts).",
    "A sub-group whose id is 'data' (Admin > Data management) is folded: its row is closed until pressed, open on its own pages, and closes again when another entry is chosen; it carries the data accent.",
    "'pageText' is the address every surface reads its administrator-edited copy from, on the page's own origin: GET for everyone, PUT for an administrator. Each group's label takes --group-label (the group's darker --accent-<id>-strong), so a heading never reads as another entry."
  ],
